# Pins for the CVAT annotation stack. Read by cvat.sh and passed to docker compose.
#
# Why pin at all: the instance was first brought up from a clone of CVAT's `develop`
# branch running `cvat/server:dev`. Both move. A `docker compose pull` on a Tuesday can
# therefore migrate the annotation database to a schema that Monday's containers cannot
# read, and there is no way back other than a restore. Annotation is the most expensive
# thing in this project per hour; it does not get to depend on an unpinned tag.
#
# To upgrade: change CVAT_VERSION here, run `./cvat.sh backup` first, then `./cvat.sh up`.
# Upstream's compose file for the tag is what defines the rest of the stack, so the tag
# and the checkout move together -- cvat.sh enforces that.
CVAT_VERSION=v2.73.0

# The hostname CVAT is reached at. It stays `localhost` because access is through an IAP
# tunnel to 127.0.0.1 rather than a published address; see docs/ANNOTATION_SETUP.md.
CVAT_HOST=localhost
